1.Find the top 5 most common log messages in Linux_2k.log using awk and sort.
Use find to list all files modified in the last 7 days.
Write a script that extracts and displays only ERROR and WARNING logs from Linux_2k.log.
sol:
sort Linux_2k.log | uniq -c | sort -nr | head -5
sudo find / -type f -mtime -7
vim log_filter.sh
echo "ERROR and WARNING Logs"
grep -Ei "ERROR|WARNING" Linux_2k.log
chmod +x log_filter.sh
./log_filter.sh
